#: src/threading/spawn.md:3
msgid ""
"**Signature**: `spawn<T>(fn: () => T): Promise<T>` — imported from `perry/"
"thread`."
msgstr ""
"**Firma**: `spawn<T>(fn: () => T): Promise<T>` — importata da `perry/thread`."

#: src/threading/spawn.md:5
msgid ""
"Runs a closure on a new OS thread and returns a Promise that resolves when "
"the thread completes. The main thread continues immediately — UI and other "
"work are not blocked."
msgstr ""
"Esegue una closure su un nuovo thread del sistema operativo e restituisce "
"una Promise che si risolve al termine del thread. Il thread principale "
"continua immediatamente — l'interfaccia utente e gli altri processi non "
"vengono bloccati."

#: src/threading/spawn.md:9
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"async function spawnBasic(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    const result = await spawn(() => {\n"
"        // This runs on a separate OS thread.\n"
"        let sum = 0\n"
"        for (let i = 0; i < 100_000_000; i++) {\n"
"            sum += i\n"
"        }\n"
"        return sum\n"
"    })\n"
"\n"
"    console.log(result) // 4999999950000000\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"async function spawnBasic(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    const result = await spawn(() => {\n"
"        // This runs on a separate OS thread.\n"
"        let sum = 0\n"
"        for (let i = 0; i < 100_000_000; i++) {\n"
"            sum += i\n"
"        }\n"
"        return sum\n"
"    })\n"
"\n"
"    console.log(result) // 4999999950000000\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:24
msgid "Non-Blocking"
msgstr "Non Bloccante"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:26
msgid "`spawn` returns immediately. The main thread doesn't wait:"
msgstr ""
"`spawn` restituisce immediatamente il controllo. Il thread principale non "
"attende:"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:28
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"async function spawnNonBlocking(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    console.log(\"1. Starting background work\")\n"
"\n"
"    const handle = spawn(() => {\n"
"        // Runs on a background thread — heavier work elided here.\n"
"        let n = 0\n"
"        for (let i = 0; i < 10_000_000; i++) n++\n"
"        return n\n"
"    })\n"
"\n"
"    console.log(\"2. Main thread continues immediately\")\n"
"\n"
"    const result = await handle\n"
"    console.log(`3. Got result: ${result}`)\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"async function spawnNonBlocking(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    console.log(\"1. Starting background work\")\n"
"\n"
"    const handle = spawn(() => {\n"
"        // Runs on a background thread — heavier work elided here.\n"
"        let n = 0\n"
"        for (let i = 0; i < 10_000_000; i++) n++\n"
"        return n\n"
"    })\n"
"\n"
"    console.log(\"2. Main thread continues immediately\")\n"
"\n"
"    const result = await handle\n"
"    console.log(`3. Got result: ${result}`)\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:53
msgid "Multiple Concurrent Tasks"
msgstr "Task Concorrenti Multipli"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:55
msgid ""
"Spawn multiple tasks and they run truly concurrently — one OS thread per "
"`spawn` call:"
msgstr ""
"Avvia più task e questi vengono eseguiti in modo veramente concorrente — un "
"thread del sistema operativo per ogni chiamata a `spawn`:"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:57
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"async function spawnMultiple(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    const t1 = spawn(() => analyseChunk(0, 1_000_000))\n"
"    const t2 = spawn(() => analyseChunk(1_000_000, 2_000_000))\n"
"    const t3 = spawn(() => analyseChunk(2_000_000, 3_000_000))\n"
"\n"
"    // All three run simultaneously on separate OS threads.\n"
"    const results = await Promise.all([t1, t2, t3])\n"
"\n"
"    console.log(`Region A: ${results[0]}`)\n"
"    console.log(`Region B: ${results[1]}`)\n"
"    console.log(`Region C: ${results[2]}`)\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"function analyseChunk(start: number, end: number): number {\n"
"    let acc = 0\n"
"    for (let i = start; i < end; i++) acc += i & 0xff\n"
"    return acc\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"async function spawnMultiple(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    const t1 = spawn(() => analyseChunk(0, 1_000_000))\n"
"    const t2 = spawn(() => analyseChunk(1_000_000, 2_000_000))\n"
"    const t3 = spawn(() => analyseChunk(2_000_000, 3_000_000))\n"
"\n"
"    // All three run simultaneously on separate OS threads.\n"
"    const results = await Promise.all([t1, t2, t3])\n"
"\n"
"    console.log(`Region A: ${results[0]}`)\n"
"    console.log(`Region B: ${results[1]}`)\n"
"    console.log(`Region C: ${results[2]}`)\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"function analyseChunk(start: number, end: number): number {\n"
"    let acc = 0\n"
"    for (let i = start; i < end; i++) acc += i & 0xff\n"
"    return acc\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:78
msgid ""
"Unlike Node.js `worker_threads`, each `spawn` is a lightweight OS thread "
"(~8MB stack), not a full V8 isolate (~2MB heap + startup cost)."
msgstr ""
"A differenza di `worker_threads` di Node.js, ogni `spawn` è un thread "
"leggero del sistema operativo (~8MB di stack), non un isolate V8 completo "
"(~2MB di heap + costo di avvio)."

#: src/threading/spawn.md:82
msgid ""
"Like `parallelMap`, `spawn` closures can capture outer variables. They are "
"deep-copied to the background thread:"
msgstr ""
"Come `parallelMap`, le closure di `spawn` possono catturare variabili "
"esterne. Queste vengono copiate in profondità nel thread in background:"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:84
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"async function spawnCapture(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    const config = { iterations: 1000, seed: 42 }\n"
"    const dataset = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]\n"
"\n"
"    const result = await spawn(() => {\n"
"        // config and dataset are deep-copied to this thread.\n"
"        let acc = config.seed\n"
"        for (let i = 0; i < config.iterations; i++) {\n"
"            acc = (acc * 1103515245 + 12345) & 0x7fffffff\n"
"        }\n"
"        for (const v of dataset) acc ^= v\n"
"        return acc\n"
"    })\n"
"\n"
"    console.log(`spawn-capture: ${result}`)\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"async function spawnCapture(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    const config = { iterations: 1000, seed: 42 }\n"
"    const dataset = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]\n"
"\n"
"    const result = await spawn(() => {\n"
"        // config and dataset are deep-copied to this thread.\n"
"        let acc = config.seed\n"
"        for (let i = 0; i < config.iterations; i++) {\n"
"            acc = (acc * 1103515245 + 12345) & 0x7fffffff\n"
"        }\n"
"        for (const v of dataset) acc ^= v\n"
"        return acc\n"
"    })\n"
"\n"
"    console.log(`spawn-capture: ${result}`)\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:103
msgid ""
"Mutable variables cannot be captured — this is enforced at compile time."
msgstr ""
"Le variabili mutabili non possono essere catturate — questo viene verificato "
"a tempo di compilazione."

#: src/threading/spawn.md:105
msgid "File System Handles"
msgstr "Handle del File System"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:107
msgid ""
"Do not capture numeric fds or `fs.promises.FileHandle` objects for file I/O "
"in `spawn`. Perry's fd registry is per thread: a numeric fd captured from "
"the main thread is not open in the worker, and a captured `FileHandle` "
"arrives detached with `fd === -1`. Capture a path string instead, then call "
"`fs.openSync` or `fs.promises.open` inside the spawned function."
msgstr ""
"Non catturare fd numerici o oggetti `fs.promises.FileHandle` per I/O su file "
"in `spawn`. Il registro dei fd di Perry è per thread: un fd numerico "
"catturato dal thread principale non è aperto nel worker, e un `FileHandle` "
"catturato arriva scollegato con `fd === -1`. Cattura invece una stringa con "
"il percorso, poi chiama `fs.openSync` o `fs.promises.open` all'interno della "
"funzione avviata con spawn."

#: src/threading/spawn.md:113
msgid "Returning Complex Values"
msgstr "Restituzione di Valori Complessi"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:115
msgid ""
"`spawn` can return any value type. Complex values (objects, arrays, strings) "
"are serialized back to the main thread automatically:"
msgstr ""
"`spawn` può restituire qualsiasi tipo di valore. I valori complessi "
"(oggetti, array, stringhe) vengono serializzati automaticamente verso il "
"thread principale:"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:141
msgid "UI Integration"
msgstr "Integrazione con l'Interfaccia Utente"

#: src/threading/spawn.md:143
msgid ""
"`spawn` is ideal for keeping native UIs responsive during heavy computation:"
msgstr ""
"`spawn` è ideale per mantenere le interfacce utente native reattive durante "
"elaborazioni intensive:"

