#: src/ui/camera.md:3
msgid ""
"The `perry/ui` module provides a live camera preview widget with color "
"sampling capabilities."
msgstr ""
"Il modulo `perry/ui` fornisce un widget di anteprima live della fotocamera "
"con capacità di campionamento del colore."

#: src/ui/camera.md:6
msgid ""
"```ts\n"
"import {\n"
"    CameraView,\n"
"    cameraStart, cameraStop,\n"
"    cameraFreeze, cameraUnfreeze,\n"
"    cameraSampleColor, cameraSetOnTap,\n"
"} from \"perry/ui\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```ts\n"
"import {\n"
"    CameraView,\n"
"    cameraStart, cameraStop,\n"
"    cameraFreeze, cameraUnfreeze,\n"
"    cameraSampleColor, cameraSetOnTap,\n"
"} from \"perry/ui\"\n"
"```"

#: src/ui/camera.md:15
msgid ""
"**Platform support:** real capture is implemented on **iOS** "
"(AVCaptureSession) and **Android** (Camera2). On **macOS**, **Linux** "
"(GTK4), **Windows**, and the **Web** target the runtime exports no-op stubs "
"so cross-platform code compiles and links cleanly — `CameraView()` returns "
"handle 0 and `cameraSampleColor` returns `-1`. Wiring real capture on those "
"platforms (AVFoundation on macOS, GStreamer/V4L2 on Linux, Media Foundation "
"on Windows, `getUserMedia` on Web) is tracked as a follow-up."
msgstr ""
"**Supporto piattaforma:** la cattura reale è implementata su **iOS** "
"(AVCaptureSession) e **Android** (Camera2). Su **macOS**, **Linux** (GTK4), "
"**Windows** e il target **Web**, il runtime esporta stub no-op in modo che "
"il codice multipiattaforma venga compilato e collegato correttamente — "
"`CameraView()` restituisce handle 0 e `cameraSampleColor` restituisce `-1`. "
"L'integrazione della cattura reale su quelle piattaforme (AVFoundation su "
"macOS, GStreamer/V4L2 su Linux, Media Foundation su Windows, `getUserMedia` "
"sul Web) è prevista come attività futura."

#: src/ui/camera.md:24 src/system/overview.md:49 src/plugins/overview.md:25
msgid "Quick Example"
msgstr "Esempio Rapido"

#: src/ui/camera.md:26
msgid ""
"```ts\n"
"const colorHex = State(\"#000000\")\n"
"\n"
"const cam = CameraView()\n"
"cameraStart(cam)\n"
"\n"
"cameraSetOnTap(cam, (x: number, y: number) => {\n"
"    const rgb = cameraSampleColor(x, y)\n"
"    if (rgb >= 0) {\n"
"        const r = Math.floor(rgb / 65536)\n"
"        const g = Math.floor((rgb % 65536) / 256)\n"
"        const b = Math.floor(rgb % 256)\n"
"        colorHex.set(`#${r.toString(16).padStart(2, \"0\")}$"
"{g.toString(16).padStart(2, \"0\")}${b.toString(16).padStart(2, \"0\")}`)\n"
"    }\n"
"})\n"
"\n"
"App({\n"
"    title: \"Color Picker\",\n"
"    width: 400,\n"
"    height: 600,\n"
"    body: VStack(16, [\n"
"        cam,\n"
"        Text(`Color: ${colorHex.value}`),\n"
"    ]),\n"
"})\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```ts\n"
"const colorHex = State(\"#000000\")\n"
"\n"
"const cam = CameraView()\n"
"cameraStart(cam)\n"
"\n"
"cameraSetOnTap(cam, (x: number, y: number) => {\n"
"    const rgb = cameraSampleColor(x, y)\n"
"    if (rgb >= 0) {\n"
"        const r = Math.floor(rgb / 65536)\n"
"        const g = Math.floor((rgb % 65536) / 256)\n"
"        const b = Math.floor(rgb % 256)\n"
"        colorHex.set(`#${r.toString(16).padStart(2, \"0\")}$"
"{g.toString(16).padStart(2, \"0\")}${b.toString(16).padStart(2, \"0\")}`)\n"
"    }\n"
"})\n"
"\n"
"App({\n"
"    title: \"Color Picker\",\n"
"    width: 400,\n"
"    height: 600,\n"
"    body: VStack(16, [\n"
"        cam,\n"
"        Text(`Color: ${colorHex.value}`),\n"
"    ]),\n"
"})\n"
"```"

