"risorsa, quindi unitevi al layout per piattaforma mostrato sopra. "
"Suggerimento CI: passare `--secret-key-b64 \"$ED25519_SECRET_KEY\"` invece "
"di `--secret-key  file` in modo che il segreto possa venire da un segreto "
"del repository senza mai colpire il filesystem del lavoratore."

#: src/updater/overview.md:237
msgid "Install + rollback flow"
msgstr "Flusso di installazione e rollback"

#: src/updater/overview.md:239
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"manifest fetch  →  semver compare  →  download to <exe>.staged\n"
"                                          ↓\n"
"                                      sha256 verify  →  ed25519 verify\n"
"                                          ↓\n"
"                                      arm sentinel (state: \"armed\")\n"
"                                          ↓\n"
"                                      install:  rename <exe> → <exe>.prev\n"
"                                                rename <exe>.staged → <exe>\n"
"                                                chmod +x   (Unix only)\n"
"                                          ↓\n"
"                                      detached relaunch  →  process.exit(0)\n"
"\n"
"next boot  →  initUpdater() reads sentinel\n"
"                  ├── healthCheckMs alive  → clearSentinel  (success)\n"
"                  ├── graceful exit         → clearSentinel  (success)\n"
"                  └── restartCount ≥ N      → performRollback + exit\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"manifest fetch  →  semver compare  →  download to <exe>.staged\n"
"                                          ↓\n"
"                                      sha256 verify  →  ed25519 verify\n"
"                                          ↓\n"
"                                      arm sentinel (state: \"armed\")\n"
"                                          ↓\n"
"                                      install:  rename <exe> → <exe>.prev\n"
"                                                rename <exe>.staged → <exe>\n"
"                                                chmod +x   (Unix only)\n"
"                                          ↓\n"
"                                      detached relaunch  →  process.exit(0)\n"
"\n"
"next boot  →  initUpdater() reads sentinel\n"
"                  ├── healthCheckMs alive  → clearSentinel  (success)\n"
"                  ├── graceful exit         → clearSentinel  (success)\n"
"                  └── restartCount ≥ N      → performRollback + exit\n"
"```"

#: src/updater/overview.md:258
msgid ""
"`installUpdate` is atomic where the OS lets us be: POSIX `rename(2)` on the "
"same filesystem, NTFS rename-while-open (the PE loader opens with "
"`FILE_SHARE_DELETE` so Windows tolerates this since Vista), and Linux's "
"mmap'd-inode-stays-alive semantics. If the staging directory ends up on a "
"different filesystem (a separate mount for `/tmp`, for instance) the rename "
"falls back to copy + remove, which has a small non-atomic window."
msgstr ""
"`installUpdate` è atomico dove il SO lo consente: `rename(2)` POSIX sullo "
"stesso filesystem, rinomina NTFS mentre il file è aperto (il PE loader apre "
"con `FILE_SHARE_DELETE` quindi Windows lo tollera da Vista), e la semantica "
"Linux di inode mappato in memoria che rimane attivo. Se la directory di "
"staging si trova su un filesystem diverso (un mount separato per `/tmp`, ad "
"esempio) la rinomina ricade su copia + rimozione, che presenta una piccola "
"finestra non atomica."

#: src/updater/overview.md:265
msgid "The sentinel is a JSON file at a per-OS user-writable path:"
msgstr ""
"Il sentinel è un file JSON in un percorso scrivibile dall'utente specifico "
"per ogni SO:"

#: src/updater/overview.md:267
msgid "Default location"
msgstr "Percorso predefinito"

#: src/updater/overview.md:269
msgid "`~/Library/Application Support/<app>/updater.sentinel`"
msgstr "`~/Library/Application Support/<app>/updater.sentinel`"

#: src/updater/overview.md:270
msgid "`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\<app>\\updater.sentinel`"
msgstr "`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\<app>\\updater.sentinel`"

#: src/updater/overview.md:271
msgid "`$XDG_STATE_HOME/<app>/updater.sentinel`"
msgstr "`$XDG_STATE_HOME/<app>/updater.sentinel`"

#: src/updater/overview.md:273
msgid ""
"`<app>` comes from the `PERRY_APP_ID` environment variable, falling back to "
"the basename of the running exe. **Set `PERRY_APP_ID` in your launch "
"environment** so the sentinel path stays stable across rename / relocation "
"of the binary."
msgstr ""
"`<app>` proviene dalla variabile d'ambiente `PERRY_APP_ID`, con fallback al "
"basename dell'eseguibile in esecuzione. **Imposta `PERRY_APP_ID` "
"nell'ambiente di avvio** in modo che il percorso del sentinel rimanga "
"stabile attraverso rinomina o spostamento del binario."

#: src/updater/overview.md:278
msgid "Low-level primitives"
msgstr "Primitive di basso livello"

#: src/updater/overview.md:280
msgid ""
"Use these when the high-level wrapper doesn't fit — custom progress UI, a "
"multi-channel manifest, an external supervisor that handles restarts, etc."
msgstr ""
"Usa queste quando il wrapper di alto livello non è adatto — UI di progresso "
"personalizzata, un manifest multi-canale, un supervisore esterno che "
"gestisce i riavvii, ecc."

#: src/updater/overview.md:283
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"import {\n"
"    compareVersions,\n"
"    verifyHash,\n"
"    verifySignature,\n"
"    computeFileSha256,\n"
"    writeSentinel,\n"
"    readSentinel,\n"
"    clearSentinel,\n"
"    getExePath,\n"
"    getBackupPath,\n"
"    getSentinelPath,\n"
"    installUpdate,\n"
"    performRollback,\n"
"    relaunch,\n"
"} from \"perry/updater\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"import {\n"
"    compareVersions,\n"
"    verifyHash,\n"
"    verifySignature,\n"
"    computeFileSha256,\n"
"    writeSentinel,\n"
"    readSentinel,\n"
"    clearSentinel,\n"
"    getExePath,\n"
"    getBackupPath,\n"
"    getSentinelPath,\n"
"    installUpdate,\n"
"    performRollback,\n"
"    relaunch,\n"
"} from \"perry/updater\"\n"
"```"

#: src/updater/overview.md:301
msgid "`compareVersions(current, candidate)`"
msgstr "`compareVersions(current, candidate)`"

#: src/updater/overview.md:303
msgid ""
"Returns `-1` (update available), `0` (equal), `1` (downgrade — never "
"offered), or `-2` (parse error). Prerelease tags handled per the semver spec."
msgstr ""
"Restituisce `-1` (aggiornamento disponibile), `0` (uguale), `1` (downgrade — "
"mai proposto), o `-2` (errore di parsing). I tag prerelease sono gestiti "
"secondo le specifiche semver."

#: src/updater/overview.md:306
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"// Returns -1 (current < candidate, update available), 0 (equal),\n"
"// 1 (current > candidate, never offered as an update), -2 (parse error).\n"
"const cmp = compareVersions(\"1.4.0\", \"1.4.1\")\n"
"if (cmp === -1) {\n"
"    console.log(\"update available\")\n"
"} else if (cmp === 0) {\n"
"    console.log(\"up to date\")\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"// Returns -1 (current < candidate, update available), 0 (equal),\n"
"// 1 (current > candidate, never offered as an update), -2 (parse error).\n"
"const cmp = compareVersions(\"1.4.0\", \"1.4.1\")\n"
"if (cmp === -1) {\n"
"    console.log(\"update available\")\n"
"} else if (cmp === 0) {\n"
"    console.log(\"up to date\")\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/updater/overview.md:317
msgid "`verifyHash` / `verifySignature` / `computeFileSha256`"
msgstr "`verifyHash` / `verifySignature` / `computeFileSha256`"

#: src/updater/overview.md:319
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"// SHA-256 + Ed25519 verification of a binary on disk. The signed payload "
"is\n"
"// the *raw 32-byte SHA-256 digest* — not the hex string and not the file\n"
"// bytes themselves. Sign side: `sha256(file) | ed25519_sign(secret_key)`.\n"
"const stagedPath = getExePath() + \".staged\"\n"
"const expectedHex = \"0123456789abcdef...\" // from your manifest\n"
"const sigB64 = \"...base64...\"             // 64-byte signature, base64\n"
"const pubB64 = \"...base64...\"             // 32-byte public key, base64\n"
"\n"
"if (verifyHash(stagedPath, expectedHex) !== 1) {\n"
"    const actual = computeFileSha256(stagedPath)\n"
"    console.error(`hash mismatch — expected ${expectedHex}, got ${actual}`)\n"
"}\n"
"if (verifySignature(stagedPath, sigB64, pubB64) !== 1) {\n"
"    console.error(\"signature verification failed\")\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"// SHA-256 + Ed25519 verification of a binary on disk. The signed payload "
"is\n"
"// the *raw 32-byte SHA-256 digest* — not the hex string and not the file\n"
"// bytes themselves. Sign side: `sha256(file) | ed25519_sign(secret_key)`.\n"
"const stagedPath = getExePath() + \".staged\"\n"
"const expectedHex = \"0123456789abcdef...\" // from your manifest\n"
"const sigB64 = \"...base64...\"             // 64-byte signature, base64\n"
"const pubB64 = \"...base64...\"             // 32-byte public key, base64\n"
"\n"
"if (verifyHash(stagedPath, expectedHex) !== 1) {\n"
"    const actual = computeFileSha256(stagedPath)\n"
"    console.error(`hash mismatch — expected ${expectedHex}, got ${actual}`)\n"
"}\n"
"if (verifySignature(stagedPath, sigB64, pubB64) !== 1) {\n"
"    console.error(\"signature verification failed\")\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/updater/overview.md:337
msgid ""
"`verifyHash` and `verifySignature` return `1` on success, `0` on any failure "
"(file missing, decode error, mismatch). `computeFileSha256` returns the hex "
"digest as a string, or `\"\"` on failure — useful for logging the _actual_ "
"hash when a `verifyHash` mismatch fires."
msgstr ""
"`verifyHash` e `verifySignature` restituiscono `1` in caso di successo, `0` "
"in caso di qualsiasi errore (file mancante, errore di decodifica, mismatch). "
"`computeFileSha256` restituisce il digest esadecimale come stringa, oppure "
"`\"\"` in caso di errore — utile per registrare l'hash _effettivo_ quando si "
"verifica un mismatch con `verifyHash`."

#: src/updater/overview.md:342
msgid "`installUpdate` / `performRollback` / `relaunch`"
msgstr "`installUpdate` / `performRollback` / `relaunch`"

#: src/updater/overview.md:344
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"// `installUpdate` atomically replaces `targetPath` with `stagedPath`,\n"
"// keeping the displaced version at `<target>.prev` for rollback.\n"
"const target = getExePath()\n"
"const staged = target + \".staged\"\n"
"\n"
"if (installUpdate(staged, target) !== 1) {\n"
"    console.error(\"install failed\")\n"
"} else {\n"
"    const pid = relaunch(target)\n"
"    if (pid < 0) {\n"
"        console.error(\"relaunch failed; restart manually\")\n"
"    } else {\n"
"        // Detached child is now running the new binary — get out of its "
"way.\n"
"        process.exit(0)\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"// `installUpdate` atomically replaces `targetPath` with `stagedPath`,\n"
"// keeping the displaced version at `<target>.prev` for rollback.\n"
"const target = getExePath()\n"
"const staged = target + \".staged\"\n"
"\n"
"if (installUpdate(staged, target) !== 1) {\n"
"    console.error(\"install failed\")\n"
"} else {\n"
"    const pid = relaunch(target)\n"
"    if (pid < 0) {\n"
"        console.error(\"relaunch failed; restart manually\")\n"
"    } else {\n"
"        // Detached child is now running the new binary — get out of its "
"way.\n"
"        process.exit(0)\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/updater/overview.md:363
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"// `performRollback` restores `<target>.prev` over `target` and moves the\n"
"// current (likely-broken) target to `<target>.broken` as a safety net.\n"
"if (performRollback(getExePath()) !== 1) {\n"
"    console.error(\"no backup to roll back to\")\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"// `performRollback` restores `<target>.prev` over `target` and moves the\n"
"// current (likely-broken) target to `<target>.broken` as a safety net.\n"
"if (performRollback(getExePath()) !== 1) {\n"
"    console.error(\"no backup to roll back to\")\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/updater/overview.md:371
msgid ""
"`relaunch` returns the child PID, or `-1` on failure. The new process is "
"fully detached (`setsid` on Unix, `DETACHED_PROCESS | "
"CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP` on Windows) so closing the current process doesn't "
"take it down."
msgstr ""
"`relaunch` restituisce il PID del processo figlio, oppure `-1` in caso di "
"errore. Il nuovo processo è completamente scollegato (`setsid` su Unix, "
"`DETACHED_PROCESS | CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP` su Windows), quindi la "
"chiusura del processo corrente non lo termina."

#: src/updater/overview.md:375
msgid "Path resolution"
msgstr "Risoluzione dei percorsi"

#: src/updater/overview.md:377
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"// Resolved per platform. macOS walks up to the surrounding `.app` bundle;\n"
"// Linux honors $APPIMAGE; Windows / bare ELF returns the canonical exe.\n"
"console.log(\"running exe   :\", getExePath())\n"
"console.log(\"backup target :\", getBackupPath())\n"
"// Sentinel path is keyed off PERRY_APP_ID — set this env var so the path\n"
"// stays stable across rename/relocation of the binary.\n"
"console.log(\"sentinel path :\", getSentinelPath())\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"// Resolved per platform. macOS walks up to the surrounding `.app` bundle;\n"
"// Linux honors $APPIMAGE; Windows / bare ELF returns the canonical exe.\n"
"console.log(\"running exe   :\", getExePath())\n"
"console.log(\"backup target :\", getBackupPath())\n"
"// Sentinel path is keyed off PERRY_APP_ID — set this env var so the path\n"
"// stays stable across rename/relocation of the binary.\n"
"console.log(\"sentinel path :\", getSentinelPath())\n"
"```"

#: src/updater/overview.md:387
msgid "`getExePath()` accounts for platform quirks:"
msgstr "`getExePath()` gestisce le peculiarità per piattaforma:"

#: src/updater/overview.md:389
msgid ""
"**macOS**: walks up to the surrounding `.app` bundle if applicable — the "
"`.app` directory is the codesign unit, so that's what you replace."
msgstr ""
"**macOS**: risale fino al bundle `.app` circostante se applicabile — la "
"directory `.app` è l'unità di codesign, quindi è quella da sostituire."

#: src/updater/overview.md:391
msgid ""
"**Linux**: honors `$APPIMAGE` when set. The AppImage runtime points "
"`current_exe()` inside a read-only squashfs mount; the real target to "
"replace is the AppImage file itself."
msgstr ""
"**Linux**: rispetta `$APPIMAGE` quando impostato. Il runtime AppImage punta "
"`current_exe()` all'interno di un mount squashfs in sola lettura; il vero "
"target da sostituire è il file AppImage stesso."

#: src/updater/overview.md:394
msgid ""
"**Windows / bare ELF / bare Mach-O**: returns the canonicalized exe path."
msgstr ""
"**Windows / bare ELF / bare Mach-O**: restituisce il percorso "
"canonicalizzato dell'eseguibile."

#: src/updater/overview.md:396
msgid "Sentinel"
msgstr "Sentinel"

#: src/updater/overview.md:398
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"// Low-level sentinel API. Most apps use `initUpdater()` from @perry/"
"updater\n"
"// instead of touching this directly, but it's here when you need it "
"(custom\n"
"// rollback policies, multi-process apps, integration with another "
"supervisor).\n"
"const sentinelPath = getSentinelPath()\n"
"writeSentinel(sentinelPath, JSON.stringify({ state: \"armed\", restartCount: "
"0 }))\n"
"const raw = readSentinel(sentinelPath)\n"
"if (raw) {\n"
"    const state = JSON.parse(raw) as { state: string; restartCount: "
"number }\n"
"    if (state.restartCount >= 2) {\n"
"        // looks like a crash loop — recover or roll back\n"
"        clearSentinel(sentinelPath)\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"// Low-level sentinel API. Most apps use `initUpdater()` from @perry/"
"updater\n"
"// instead of touching this directly, but it's here when you need it "
"(custom\n"
"// rollback policies, multi-process apps, integration with another "
"supervisor).\n"
"const sentinelPath = getSentinelPath()\n"
"writeSentinel(sentinelPath, JSON.stringify({ state: \"armed\", restartCount: "
"0 }))\n"
"const raw = readSentinel(sentinelPath)\n"
"if (raw) {\n"
"    const state = JSON.parse(raw) as { state: string; restartCount: "
"number }\n"
"    if (state.restartCount >= 2) {\n"
"        // looks like a crash loop — recover or roll back\n"
"        clearSentinel(sentinelPath)\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/updater/overview.md:414
msgid ""
"`writeSentinel` is atomic (tmp file + rename), creates the parent directory "
"if needed, and returns `1` on success / `0` on any IO error. `clearSentinel` "
"is idempotent — returns `1` whether the file existed or not."
msgstr ""
"`writeSentinel` è atomico (file temporaneo + rinomina), crea la directory "
"padre se necessario e restituisce `1` in caso di successo / `0` per "
"qualsiasi errore di IO. `clearSentinel` è idempotente — restituisce `1` "
"indipendentemente dal fatto che il file esistesse o meno."

#: src/updater/overview.md:418
msgid "What's not here (yet)"
msgstr "Cosa non è ancora presente"

#: src/updater/overview.md:420
msgid ""
"**UI primitives** — a \"Restart now\" modal with `ProgressView` belongs "
"inside `perry/ui` proper rather than the updater package. Tracked as a "
"follow-up."
msgstr ""
"**Primitive UI** — un modal \"Riavvia ora\" con `ProgressView` appartiene a "
"`perry/ui` vero e proprio piuttosto che al pacchetto updater. Tracciato come "
"follow-up."

#: src/updater/overview.md:423
msgid ""
"**Privileged install** for system-wide locations (`/Applications`, `Program "
"Files`). The current install path only handles user-writable locations (`~/"
"Applications`, `~/.local/bin`, `%LOCALAPPDATA%`). UAC / `SMJobBless` is a "
"separate concern."
msgstr ""
"**Installazione con privilegi elevati** per percorsi di sistema (`/"
"Applications`, `Program Files`). Il percorso di installazione attuale "
"gestisce solo le posizioni scrivibili dall'utente (`~/Applications`, "
"`~/.local/bin`, `%LOCALAPPDATA%`). UAC / `SMJobBless` è una problematica "
"separata."

#: src/updater/overview.md:427
msgid ""
"**Delta updates** (bsdiff), **multi-channel** (stable / beta), **staged "
"rollouts**."
msgstr ""
"**Aggiornamenti delta** (bsdiff), **multi-canale** (stable / beta), "
"**rollout graduali**."

#: src/updater/overview.md:429
msgid ""
"**Notarization / code-signing** during install. Binaries are expected to "
"arrive already signed; the updater doesn't try to be a notarization tool."
msgstr ""
"**Notarizzazione / firma del codice** durante l'installazione. Si prevede "
"che i binari arrivino già firmati; l'updater non tenta di essere uno "
"strumento di notarizzazione."

#: src/updater/overview.md:432
msgid "Testing your update flow"
msgstr "Testare il flusso di aggiornamento"

#: src/updater/overview.md:434
msgid ""
"The crate ships smoke-test scripts that exercise verify → install → relaunch "
"end-to-end against a real Perry binary:"
msgstr ""
"Il crate include script di smoke test che esercitano il flusso verify → "
